 went against the  will of his scientists this is  definitely a political decision and of  course in the end the scientists are  there to give advice and political  decisions are made but let me stress  again the economics point in exactly the  same way it's not as if the economists  should be saying come on guys stop they  lock down let's get back to business  without knowing that we can get this  under control  everyone must see that the sooner we get  it under control the sooner we get the  economy back up and running the sooner  we get schools officer shops restaurants  pubs etc open but I tell you what I'm  really worried about and this is what  every scientist is worried about around  the whole world ninety seven percent of  what's called super spreading events  occur indoors and if we're saying we're  going to open up restaurants and in  particular pubs I think that's where the  big risk lies because we all know two  things one is the pub's do get quite  crowded now they will try to keep to  even the one meter rule but as you as  the evening goes on and people get  happier and merrier we all know what  happens we all relax and one meter apart  is the distance the social distance  average that we stand up between each  other but when we're talking we use  people and when we use body language we  narrow that distance down there were  very firm warnings they were there from  the prime minister and the scientific  advisors yesterday that we really do  need to stick to the guidance it is two  metres wherever possible one meter plus  with mitigations can I ask you about the  different approaches though between the  different nations of the United Kingdom  they're all seeing the same science the  chief medical officer  that he was in constant contact with the  chief medical officers of Wales Scotland  and Northern Ireland so why are we  seeing these different approaches quite  simply different political decisions I'm  sure I don't I don't think that there's  a disagreement across the borders about  the the science and how risky it is to  change the strategy at this point in  time I mean one thing I can say is that  the the Prime Minister made very clear  statements about the fact that the  government is going to keep an eye on  whether or not this results in a super  spread event I need to worry it though  about the statement about localities in  other words if we say right in Liverpool  there's a super spread event there for  Liverpool goes back into lockdown I'm  afraid there is really it's difficult to  understand a local spread event in a  country where movement of people around  the country is happening in other words  it's likely that if it begins locally in  one part of the country it will spread  okay so David King thank you very much  indeed for your thoughts this morning  thank you
 

